    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d622">

                <pb facs="0662" n="648" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg648"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.852/90: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-17T20:00:00-03:00">February 17,
                            1944—8 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:19 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>606. Department’s 530, February 16, 7 p.m.<anchor n="44" xml:id="d622-f1"/> The
                    Embassy and Brazilian Maritime Commission are in agreement. Foreign Office is
                    sending text to President Vargas for his approval. The Embassy requests
                    telegraphic authority to exchange notes with Foreign Office based upon the text
                    reported in the Embassy’s airgram 303 February 17, 2 p.m.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
